<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20870] sanity test_315: FAIL: multiop still running</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20870</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_315 forks a background multiop reader, sleeps 2s, reads /proc/$PID/io, then sends kill -USR1 $PID without waiting for it to exit. run_one()'s post-test 'ps auxww | grep multiop' check (test-framework.sh:8034) can still see the process in the brief window between the signal and its actual exit, failing the test with no real hang.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/148a1bbc-1af8-47ad-9558-5bc341dcd2b6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/148a1bbc-1af8-47ad-9558-5bc341dcd2b6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/593207e3-ef0a-4791-ba06-58ce05156b03" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/593207e3-ef0a-4791-ba06-58ce05156b03&lt;/a&gt; (change 53518 patchset 17, review-ldiskfs-arm, aarch64)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not this patch's: change 53518 PS17 only touches lustre/tests/test-framework.sh's format_mgs/format_mdt/format_ost/parallel_start/parallel_wait/do_node helpers (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17240" title="change test-framework to format and mount targets in parallel " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17240"&gt;LU-17240&lt;/a&gt;, parallel target formatting). test_315 itself is unmodified (last touched by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10929" title="skip sanity/315 if IO accounting is not supported" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10929"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10929&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; years ago) and does not call formatall or any of the parallel-format helpers; the suite log shows no formatting activity near test_315, which ran and failed in 17s with no sign of a hang. test_315 has no history of this failure on master or lustre-reviews in the last 90 days (one occurrence only), and no existing LU ticket names test_315's multiop race specifically (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-4671" title="sanity test_43: multiop still running" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-4671"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-4671&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12713" title="sanityn test_51a: FAIL: multiop is still there" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12713"&gt;LU-12713&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18124" title="sanityn test_51a: multiop is still there" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18124"&gt;LU-18124&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15631" title="recovery-small test_21d: multiop still running" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15631"&gt;LU-15631&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20767" title="recovery-small test_21d: @@@@@@ FAIL: multiop still running " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20767"&gt;LU-20767&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14773" title="reduce run_one() overhead" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14773"&gt;LU-14773&lt;/a&gt; cover the same ps-check race in other tests, not this one).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-53518-ps17-6c7e6af2b5ed on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/53518" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/53518&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
